                <pb facs="0212" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v26/pg186"/>

                <head>34. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On April 11, 1974, three members of the Popular Front for the Liberation of
                    Palestine-General Command attacked the Israeli town of Kiryat Shmona near the
                    border with Lebanon. The PFLP–GC members killed eighteen Israeli civilians in an
                    apartment building, and all three attackers were later killed that day by
                    Israeli forces in a shootout. (<hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi>,
                    April 12, 1974, p. 65) On April 12, Israel launched retaliatory attacks against
                    six Lebanese villages bordering Israel and destroyed the houses of residents
                    suspected of sheltering Arab guerrillas. (Ibid., April 13, 1974, p. 1)</p>
            </div>
